Augury is the practice of looking into the future, described as looking too far down the world tree. Augurs in [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]] must keep within strict allotments on how much future-telling they do, a law in place since the Incident of 24, when overuse was blamed for harming the whole continent.

The blowback from excessive augury is not always the same. Past cases have brought darkness for days or trouble moving from one part of the [[Infinite Horizon|Horizon]] to another. The [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]] treated the endless rain that fell over [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] as one such symptom, and Major-Chaplain [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Ewan McFoster|Ewan McFoster]] is sure the loss of Star 13 at [[Geography/Velthara/index|Tor's Strand]] came from the same cause.

Soothsayers use decks of cards bearing the likenesses of the [[Hierophant|hierophants]] as a medium for future-telling. The [[Org/The Sears/index|Sears]] keep an oracular device that forecasts the weather over Hallia.

The convox held that the endless rain was itself a corrective measure: the illegal augurs worked out of the sewers, and flooding them drove the augurs to move.
